Use isolated mode for final stage acceptance where appropriate.

Never modify the kickoff repository, official specifications, harness, or shipped checks.

============================================================
FACTORY ROSTER
============================================================

Lead / release control:
@[[9d100079-435e-4250-991c-3bb673977719]]

Specification analysis:
@nurali6002217/contract-auditor

Core implementation:
@nurali6002217/systems-engineer

Product / browser experience:
@nurali6002217/experience-engineer

Independent verification:
@nurali6002217/adversarial-verifier

Confirm all five configured seats are present before the first delegated handoff.

============================================================
PRIMARY OBJECTIVE
============================================================

Autonomously produce and independently accept:

stage-1/
stage-2/
stage-3/
stage-4/

Each stage folder must be a complete standalone buildable service implementing exactly its cumulative specification.

Stage 1: Stage 1 only.
Stage 2: Stage 1 + Stage 2.
Stage 3: Stage 1 + Stage 2 + Stage 3.
Stage 4: Stage 1 + Stage 2 + Stage 3 + Stage 4.

Complete all four stages unless an objective blocker makes progress impossible.

The written specifications are the source of truth.

Do not optimize merely for the visible harness.

Target:
- hidden-test-resistant correctness;
- strong autonomous collaboration;
- maintainable production engineering;
- exceptional product quality;
- reproducible evidence;
- full four-stage completion.

============================================================
AUTONOMY
============================================================

Do not ask the human operator for clarification, approval, confirmation, debugging help, architecture decisions, permission to repair, permission to retry, or permission to continue.

Do not pause waiting for human input.

Resolve decisions from:
1. specification;
2. repository state;
3. evidence;
4. independent reasoning;
5. collaboration between seats.

If blocked, attempt autonomous recovery and record the blocker truthfully.

No additional human message should be required until your final completion report.

============================================================
SELF-CONTAINED HANDOFFS
============================================================

Every delegated seat must receive a self-contained assignment.

A handoff must provide enough information to execute without inspecting unrelated room history.

Include:
- objective;
- complete cumulative requirements needed by that seat;
- ownership;
- constraints;
- deliverables;
- acceptance conditions;
- required evidence;
- exact revision where applicable.

For each stage, read the authoritative spec files and transmit the complete required cumulative specification to delegated seats.

Do not substitute:
"read the file",
"see above",
"read the room",
or a message reference
for the complete handoff.

Long handoffs may be split into clearly numbered parts.

============================================================
SPEC-TO-EVIDENCE PROCESS
============================================================

For every stage:

1. Contract Auditor derives one canonical atomic requirements ledger and risk model.

2. Identify CRITICAL/HIGH obligations, precedence, concurrency, retries, atomicity, temporal rules, authorization, historical truth, migration, no-op behavior, ordering and important feature interactions where applicable.

3. Production ownership is assigned explicitly.

4. Production owners implement specification semantics, commit coherent work and report FULL commit SHAs.

5. Establish one exact integration production SHA.

6. Independent Verifier verifies that exact immutable revision independently.

7. Verification includes applicable:
- official harness;
- black-box specification checks;
- robustness/boundary validation;
- validation/error precedence;
- concurrency validation;
- retry/replay behavior;
- atomic rollback;
- temporal/history behavior;
- metamorphic checks;
- independent oracle/model checks for high-risk deterministic semantics;
- prior-stage regression;
- required upgrade/state-transfer paths;
- isolated clean execution.

8. Independent Verifier issues formal ACCEPT or REJECT tied to the exact production SHA.

9. Genuine product REJECT:
owner reproduces → root-cause repair → NEW SHA → independent re-verification.

No seat accepts its own production work.

============================================================
ACCEPTANCE AND EFFICIENCY
============================================================

Correctness is mandatory, but repeated evidence bureaucracy is not useful.

Use coarse meaningful work units.

Prefer per stage:
- ONE canonical requirements ledger;
- ONE coherent implementation result per owner revision;
- ONE consolidated verification campaign/report per tested production revision;
- ONE formal verdict;
- ONE release attestation.

Create supplemental evidence only when it:
- closes a concrete uncovered CRITICAL/HIGH requirement;
- investigates a reproducible defect;
- validates a NEW production revision;
- satisfies a required compatibility/regression gate;
- resolves a genuine blocker.

Once an exact production SHA has formal independent ACCEPT and required CRITICAL/HIGH obligations are closed:

FREEZE ACCEPTANCE EVIDENCE.

Do not continue cosmetic graph reconciliation, bindings, comparisons, addenda or duplicate checkpoints.

The Conductor must advance to the next permitted stage within one coordination cycle after acceptance unless a concrete blocking requirement gap exists.

Do not create a separate conversational task for every individual test or assertion. Batch related checks into executable verification campaigns.

Chat volume and task count are not objectives.

============================================================
FAILURE CLASSIFICATION
============================================================

Classify material failures as:

PRODUCT DEFECT
VERIFIER DEFECT
INFRASTRUCTURE DEFECT
INCONCLUSIVE

Do not modify production code for verifier or infrastructure failures.

For tool/runtime/process interruptions:
- preserve the pinned SHA;
- preserve valid completed evidence;
- recover from the last proven checkpoint;
- re-establish required execution environment;
- continue autonomously.

Use neutral engineering language:
independent verification,
robustness validation,
boundary validation,
stress scenario,
controlled calibration.

If a benign verification turn is interrupted by a classifier/runtime, preserve state, rephrase the legitimate objective neutrally and continue.

============================================================
EXACT-SHA VERIFICATION
============================================================

Never independently accept a mutable shared HEAD.

Verification must target an exact FULL production SHA.

Use a clean immutable materialization of that exact SHA.

Avoid Windows/WSL linked-worktree pointer problems.

Prefer disposable Linux-native verification materialization where useful.

Keep production revisions and evidence-only commits clearly distinct.

============================================================
VERIFICATION INFRASTRUCTURE
============================================================

Before expensive verification:
- confirm Docker/runtime availability;
- confirm target SHA;
- clean stale verifier containers/resources;
- ensure sufficient resources;
- use unique runtime resources;
- prefer runtime-assigned or proven-usable host ports;
- respect the specification's actual readiness and request budgets.

Do not reject compliant production because the verifier invented a stricter timeout.

Raw diagnostics remain outside the submission repository when possible.

============================================================
EVIDENCE SAFETY
============================================================

Never commit:
- API keys;
- access tokens;
- passwords;
- secrets;
- credential-bearing URLs;
- raw environment dumps;
- unnecessary environment assignments.

Repository evidence must be sanitized.

Before evidence commits, scan for credential-shaped material.

============================================================
STAGE PROGRESSION
============================================================

After Stage N receives formal independent ACCEPT:

1. freeze stage-N;
2. preserve it unchanged;
3. copy its complete service into stage-(N+1);
4. ensure no nested .git exists;
5. establish a committed next-stage baseline;
6. extend ONLY the new stage folder.

Do not implement later-stage answers backwards into earlier folders.

If new material evidence proves an earlier acceptance wrong, reopen it explicitly and preserve the audit trail.

============================================================
TABLEKEEPER QUALITY EXPECTATIONS
============================================================

The Contract Auditor and Independent Verifier must derive concrete cases from the complete authoritative specs themselves.

At minimum recognize the broad risk surfaces across the four stages:

Stage 1:
concurrency-sensitive occupancy, retry/idempotency semantics, atomic changes, validation precedence, authentication/privacy, time zones/DST, state export/import.

Stage 2:
all Stage 1 regression, presentation-quality responsive browser UX, asynchronous races, uncertain/lost responses, combined resources, concurrency and Stage 1→2 continuity.

Stage 3:
all prior regression, effective-dated semantics, historical truth, revisions/no-ops, recurring state, per-occurrence semantics and required earlier-stage upgrades.

Stage 4:
all prior regression, atomic operational replanning, exact deterministic optimization, preview/application staleness, recurring amendments, concurrency and all required populated-state upgrade paths.

These themes are NOT an exhaustive checklist and do not replace independent reading of the full specifications.

============================================================
PRODUCT QUALITY
============================================================

From browser scope onward, build a coherent presentation-ready hospitality product.

Required semantics and test hooks are non-negotiable.

Target:
- premium visual hierarchy;
- human-readable restaurant/seating information;
- responsive 375px and desktop UX;
- accessibility and keyboard usability;
- clear loading/empty/error/success/uncertain states;
- stale-response protection;
- correct lost-response recovery;
- locally bundled runtime assets;
- maintainable component structure.

Do not turn the primary product into a testing dashboard.

After required correctness is secure, high-value optional presentation improvements may be added when they improve judging value without risking required behavior.

Strong optional examples:
- manager resilience/replanning visualization;
- readable reservation/history provenance;
- secondary reliability/proof view demonstrating selected verified properties.

Do not add unrelated gimmicks or runtime dependencies.

============================================================
INDEPENDENT ORACLE / CONCURRENCY / UPGRADES
============================================================

Where useful and bounded:

- create an independently derived behavioral/reference oracle for high-risk deterministic semantics;
- use metamorphic verification for specification-supported equivalences;
- use coordinated overlapping operations for concurrency-sensitive behavior;
- compare observed outcomes to permitted sequential behavior where required.

By Stage 4 maintain evidence for every upgrade path required by the specifications.

Do not reuse production decision logic inside an alleged independent oracle.

============================================================
GIT / PROVENANCE
============================================================

Maintain readable Git history.

Every meaningful production or repair result must report a FULL commit SHA.

Do not squash or amend away meaningful collaboration history.

Do not hide failed attempts that materially informed repairs.

Keep a traceable chain:

ROOM HANDOFF
→ OWNER
→ PRODUCTION SHA
→ INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION
→ VERDICT

============================================================
FINAL RUN AUDIT
============================================================

Do not stop after Stage 1, 2 or 3.

After Stage 4 ACCEPT:

- run cumulative official checks across all stage folders;
- confirm every folder claims exactly its intended stage;
- confirm each stage is independently buildable;
- confirm lower accepted stages remained preserved;
- confirm no nested .git directories exist;
- confirm isolated/offline runtime requirements;
- confirm repository state is coherent;
- confirm no unresolved CRITICAL/HIGH product defect;
- confirm required upgrade paths;
- confirm evidence is sanitized;
- confirm exact production SHAs are recorded;
- confirm no human steering occurred after this dispatch.

============================================================
FINAL REPORT
============================================================

When the complete run is finished, send one final completion report to the human operator containing:

- overall outcome;
- accepted FULL production SHA for each stage;
- official harness result for each stage;
- cumulative regression status;
- meaningful contribution of every seat;
- architecture decisions and rationale;
- CRITICAL/HIGH risk coverage;
- meaningful defect(s) caught by independent review;
- REJECT → repair → re-verification cycles;
- independent robustness verification;
- concurrency evidence;
- oracle/model/metamorphic evidence where used;
- upgrade-continuity results;
- UI/product-quality work;
- optional differentiators completed;
- runtime/infrastructure recoveries;
- evidence-safety status;
- measured elapsed time if available;
- actual model/spend information if available;
- known limitations;
- unresolved blockers;
- explicit confirmation whether ANY additional human input was required.

Do not invent results or metrics.

============================================================
BEGIN
============================================================

Begin now.

First:
1. perform environment/repository preflight;
2. confirm all five configured seats are present;
3. independently read the complete Stage 1 specification;
4. deliver the complete self-contained Stage 1 contract-analysis handoff to @nurali6002217/contract-auditor.

Continue autonomously through Stage 4.

